const TEST_SECONDS = 15 * 60;
const PASSAGES = [{"id":1,"level":"B1–B1+","title":"Passage 1 — Four Ways To Be A Careful Shopper","teacherTitle":"Four Ways To Be A Careful Shopper","wordCountTarget":null,"paragraphs":["People sometimes say that good shopping means finding the lowest price. Four residents of Can Tho, however, explain why their decisions depend on more than a number on a price tag.","Mai, a university student, receives a small amount of pocket money each week. After paying for bus journeys and lunch, she puts by some money for a camera. When a shop advertises a discount, she compares the offer with prices at two other stores. Before going to a shopping centre, she writes down what she actually needs. This helps her resist advertisements for products that look attractive but would not solve any practical problem. She has learned that a product on sale is not necessarily a bargain. “A cheap purchase is expensive if it never gets used,” she says. Once she almost bought a colourful jacket simply because it was half price. Instead, she went window shopping with a friend and discovered that she did not really want it.","Nam repairs bicycles for a living. He often buys tools from second-hand markets because a well-made older tool can be more valuable to him than a new but weak one. Before buying anything, he checks whether it is in good condition and whether replacement parts are available. His customers sometimes bring in bicycles that appear too old to repair. He shows them the cost of repair and the cost of replacement so they can choose. “The initial price matters, but the years of service matter too,” he explains. Nam recently repaired a neighbour's bicycle for far less than the cost of purchasing a new one.","Lan manages a small food shop. She buys fresh products from several farmers and selects suppliers who offer reliable delivery, not just low prices. If a supplier charges very little but sends damaged vegetables, she may lose both money and customers. Last month, a delivery of fruit arrived in bad condition. Lan kept the receipt and asked for a refund rather than passing the damaged products on to shoppers. She believes that honest service encourages people to return. Her regular customers appreciate that she explains changes in prices instead of hiding them.","Finally, Khoa works at a student advice centre. He helps young adults make budgets and understand the difference between a loan and money they already own. He often hears students say that they can afford an item because their debit card payment was accepted. Khoa points out that a successful payment does not prove that the purchase fits their monthly budget. He asks students to record small expenses each evening. This habit makes repeated purchases easier to notice. In his view, financial confidence develops through small, practical decisions rather than a single clever bargain.","These four shoppers have different incomes and needs, yet they share one principle: price is only part of value. A careful customer considers usefulness, quality, service and future expenses before making a purchase."],"references":[{"p":2,"start":412,"end":416,"text":"they"},{"p":4,"start":418,"end":428,"text":"This habit"}],"questions":[{"n":1,"displayN":1,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What does Mai mean by saying, “A cheap purchase is expensive if it never gets used”?","options":{"A":"An unused item is poor value even when its price is low.","B":"Shops should increase the price of products on sale.","C":"Every discounted item will become more valuable later.","D":"Buying an expensive item is always the safest choice."},"answer":"A","type":"Restatement","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"A cheap purchase is expensive if it never gets used"}],"evidenceExplanation":"A cheap purchase is expensive if it never gets used","viExplanation":"Giá thấp không đồng nghĩa với đáng tiền. Nếu mua về mà không sử dụng, món hàng vẫn là một khoản chi tiêu lãng phí."},{"n":2,"displayN":2,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What can be inferred about Mai’s shopping habits?","options":{"A":"She buys clothes whenever she sees a large discount.","B":"She never visits stores without a fixed list.","C":"She usually considers purchases rather than acting immediately.","D":"She believes all online advertisements are dishonest."},"answer":"C","type":"Inference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"she compares the offer with prices at two other stores"},{"p":1,"text":"she did not really want it"}],"evidenceExplanation":"she compares the offer with prices at two other stores she did not really want it","viExplanation":"Mai so sánh giá và cân nhắc nhu cầu thực tế, vì thế có thể suy ra cô không mua hàng chỉ vì thấy giảm giá."},{"n":3,"displayN":3,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The word “bargain” in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":{"A":"a product with no return policy","B":"an item that offers unusually good value","C":"a payment made with a debit card","D":"a purchase made without a receipt"},"answer":"B","type":"Vocabulary","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"a product on sale is not necessarily a bargain"}],"evidenceExplanation":"a product on sale is not necessarily a bargain","viExplanation":"Bargain chỉ một món hời, tức hàng hóa có giá trị tốt so với số tiền bỏ ra, chứ không đơn thuần là món hàng được giảm giá."},{"n":4,"displayN":4,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What does Nam mean by saying that “the years of service matter too”?","options":{"A":"The age of a customer determines the price.","B":"Repair shops should sell only the newest tools.","C":"Old bicycles should always be replaced immediately.","D":"A product’s useful life affects whether it is worth buying."},"answer":"D","type":"Restatement","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"The initial price matters, but the years of service matter too"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The initial price matters, but the years of service matter too","viExplanation":"Nam nhấn mạnh độ bền và thời gian sử dụng hữu ích của sản phẩm cũng quyết định giá trị mua sắm."},{"n":5,"displayN":5,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The word “they” in “so they can choose” refers to ______.","options":{"A":"Nam’s customers","B":"replacement parts","C":"second-hand markets","D":"bicycle repairers"},"answer":"A","type":"Reference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"He shows them the cost of repair and the cost of replacement so they can choose"}],"evidenceExplanation":"He shows them the cost of repair and the cost of replacement so they can choose","viExplanation":"Đại từ “they” thay thế cho những khách hàng mà Nam đang tư vấn hai phương án sửa hoặc thay xe."},{"n":6,"displayN":6,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The word “valuable” in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":{"A":"difficult to repair","B":"expensive to transport","C":"useful or worth a great deal to someone","D":"available only in a luxury shop"},"answer":"C","type":"Vocabulary","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"a well-made older tool can be more valuable to him than a new but weak one"}],"evidenceExplanation":"a well-made older tool can be more valuable to him than a new but weak one","viExplanation":"Trong ngữ cảnh này, valuable nghĩa là hữu ích hoặc có giá trị đáng kể với người dùng, không nhất thiết phải đắt tiền."},{"n":7,"displayN":7,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What did Lan do when damaged fruit arrived?","options":{"A":"She sold it at a lower price.","B":"She asked for a refund and kept the receipt.","C":"She exchanged it for new kitchen equipment.","D":"She gave it away without informing customers."},"answer":"B","type":"Factual","evidencePhrases":[{"p":3,"text":"Lan kept the receipt and asked for a refund"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Lan kept the receipt and asked for a refund","viExplanation":"Bài đọc nêu trực tiếp Lan giữ hóa đơn rồi yêu cầu hoàn tiền khi nhận trái cây hỏng."},{"n":8,"displayN":8,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which conclusion about Lan is best supported by the passage?","options":{"A":"She would prefer the cheapest supplier regardless of quality.","B":"She avoids discussing price changes with regular customers.","C":"She depends entirely on advertising to attract customers.","D":"She values reliable suppliers and long-term customer trust."},"answer":"D","type":"Inference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":3,"text":"selects suppliers who offer reliable delivery, not just low prices"},{"p":3,"text":"honest service encourages people to return"}],"evidenceExplanation":"selects suppliers who offer reliable delivery, not just low prices honest service encourages people to return","viExplanation":"Lan ưu tiên nhà cung cấp đáng tin cậy và quan hệ lâu dài với khách hàng; không chỉ quan tâm đến giá rẻ."},{"n":9,"displayN":9,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The phrase “This habit” in paragraph 5 refers to ______.","options":{"A":"using a debit card for every purchase","B":"asking a bank for a larger loan","C":"recording small expenses each evening","D":"buying goods only when they are on sale"},"answer":"C","type":"Reference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":4,"text":"He asks students to record small expenses each evening. This habit makes repeated purchases easier to notice"}],"evidenceExplanation":"He asks students to record small expenses each evening. This habit makes repeated purchases easier to notice","viExplanation":"Cụm “This habit” chỉ hành động ghi lại các khoản chi nhỏ vào mỗi tối ở ngay câu trước."},{"n":10,"displayN":10,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What is the main purpose of the passage?","options":{"A":"To illustrate different ways people judge the value of purchases","B":"To prove that second-hand products are always superior","C":"To encourage every shopper to use a single payment method","D":"To explain the legal process of returning faulty products"},"answer":"A","type":"Purpose","evidencePhrases":[{"p":5,"text":"price is only part of value"},{"p":5,"text":"A careful customer considers usefulness, quality, service and future expenses"}],"evidenceExplanation":"price is only part of value A careful customer considers usefulness, quality, service and future expenses","viExplanation":"Bốn ví dụ minh họa các cách đánh giá giá trị hàng hóa, cho thấy mua sắm hợp lý cần xét nhiều yếu tố ngoài giá bán."},{"n":51,"displayN":1,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"This helps her resist advertisements for products that look attractive but would not solve any practical problem.\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"It prevents her from visiting shopping centres altogether.","B":"It helps her avoid tempting products that she does not actually need.","C":"It encourages her to spend more on attractive products.","D":"It makes advertisements easier for her to remember."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: It helps her avoid tempting products that she does not actually need.","viExplanation":""},{"n":52,"displayN":2,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a product on sale is not necessarily a bargain\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"A discounted product may still be poor value for money.","B":"Discounts are never offered on worthwhile products.","C":"Every reduced item is cheaper than similar products elsewhere.","D":"All sale items must be purchased immediately."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A discounted product may still be poor value for money.","viExplanation":""},{"n":53,"displayN":3,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"she did not really want it\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"She was disappointed by the size of the jacket.","B":"She lacked enough money to buy the jacket.","C":"She realised she had no genuine interest in owning the jacket.","D":"She had already purchased an identical jacket."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: She realised she had no genuine interest in owning the jacket.","viExplanation":""},{"n":54,"displayN":4,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a well-made older tool can be more valuable to him than a new but weak one\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"He prefers every used tool regardless of quality.","B":"An inexpensive new tool always works longer.","C":"He buys old tools only because new tools are unavailable.","D":"Durable second-hand equipment can be worth more than low-quality new equipment."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Durable second-hand equipment can be worth more than low-quality new equipment.","viExplanation":""},{"n":55,"displayN":5,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"whether replacement parts are available\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Whether the tool has been advertised online.","B":"Whether components can be obtained if a repair is needed.","C":"Whether a store accepts only cash payments.","D":"Whether every part is supplied free of charge."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Whether components can be obtained if a repair is needed.","viExplanation":""},{"n":56,"displayN":6,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"she may lose both money and customers\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Unreliable supplies could damage her income and her customer base.","B":"She is guaranteed to increase sales if supplies are cheap.","C":"Her customers are required to cover all losses.","D":"She can save money by ignoring product quality."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Unreliable supplies could damage her income and her customer base.","viExplanation":""},{"n":57,"displayN":7,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"honest service encourages people to return\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Giving every customer a discount eliminates complaints.","B":"Advertising is more important than the quality of service.","C":"Transparent and fair treatment helps retain customers.","D":"Customers return only when they have no alternatives."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Transparent and fair treatment helps retain customers.","viExplanation":""},{"n":58,"displayN":8,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a successful payment does not prove that the purchase fits their monthly budget\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Card approval confirms that an item is essential.","B":"Every debit card transaction increases personal savings.","C":"People who use debit cards never need a budget.","D":"Being able to pay now does not mean the item is affordable within one's plan."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Being able to pay now does not mean the item is affordable within one's plan.","viExplanation":""},{"n":59,"displayN":9,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"This habit makes repeated purchases easier to notice\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Recording small expenses helps people identify patterns of spending.","B":"Making frequent purchases becomes completely impossible.","C":"People should stop keeping a record of spending.","D":"A bank automatically cancels repeated charges."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Recording small expenses helps people identify patterns of spending.","viExplanation":""},{"n":60,"displayN":10,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"price is only part of value\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The cheapest product must be the highest-quality one.","B":"A product's worth depends on more than its price alone.","C":"Customers should avoid considering service or durability.","D":"Price becomes irrelevant whenever an item is on sale."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A product's worth depends on more than its price alone.","viExplanation":""}]},{"id":2,"level":"B1+–B2","title":"Passage 2 — The Real Cost Of A Pop-Up Shop","teacherTitle":"The Real Cost Of A Pop-Up Shop","wordCountTarget":null,"paragraphs":["A pop-up shop allows a small business to sell goods for a short period without signing a long rental contract. For inexperienced sellers, a trial period may seem like a low-risk way to discover whether customers appreciate their products before investing their savings in a permanent location. Such shops are popular with student designers and local food producers, but an inexpensive-looking advert for space can hide significant expenses.","When Riverside Shopping Centre offered ten stalls for a four-week trial, it advertised a rent of 450 dollars per stall. The amount seemed reasonable compared with the cost of a permanent shop. Applicants soon discovered, however, that they also needed to pay a refundable deposit of 200 dollars. The deposit would be returned after the trial if the stall was left in good condition and all outstanding charges were settled. [A] Insurance, electricity and a share of the weekend cleaning service were separate expenses. [B] Some applicants had expected the rent to cover everything, so the additional costs changed their budgets. [C] The centre explained that the deposit was held as security rather than counted as income from selling space. [D]","The centre's manager, Ms Le, did not believe that a lower headline price automatically represented better value for money. She compared two locations. The entrance offered heavy foot traffic but had high delivery charges and little storage space. A quieter corridor was less expensive to operate and provided secure storage. Several sellers chose the corridor even though fewer visitors would pass their stalls. They expected that customers looking specifically for handmade products would still find them through online adverts.","A survey from the previous year suggested that approximately seventy percent of visitors who came to weekend craft events had checked stall information online before travelling. Ms Le included this figure in the information pack to explain why location within the centre might be less important than it first appeared. She also advised sellers to compare their likely earnings with all expenses, including packaging and card-payment fees, before deciding whether the project could make a profit.","Applicants reacted differently. Some were disappointed that cleaning and electricity were not included. Others were relieved to learn that the deposit was refundable. A few worried that online adverts would not bring enough customers to the quieter corridor. Nonetheless, the manager remained cautiously optimistic. She encouraged applicants to ask questions and study a written breakdown of costs rather than choose the cheapest-looking offer immediately.","The trial demonstrated a broader lesson about business decisions. A low advertised price may attract attention, but a realistic budget requires more than one figure. Sellers who understand what they must pay, what they might earn and which risks they can manage are better placed to decide whether a temporary shop is genuinely worth the investment."],"references":[{"p":1,"start":585,"end":605,"text":"the additional costs"}],"questions":[{"n":11,"displayN":11,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which title best summarises the passage?","options":{"A":"How to advertise a permanent luxury store","B":"Why online shopping is replacing physical stores","C":"Understanding the full costs of temporary retail space","D":"The history of Riverside Shopping Centre"},"answer":"C","type":"Main Idea","evidencePhrases":[{"p":0,"text":"an inexpensive-looking advert for space can hide significant expenses"},{"p":5,"text":"a realistic budget requires more than one figure"}],"evidenceExplanation":"an inexpensive-looking advert for space can hide significant expenses a realistic budget requires more than one figure","viExplanation":"Toàn bài phân tích chi phí thực tế của cửa hàng tạm thời và cách lập ngân sách, phù hợp nhất với nhan đề về tổng chi phí."},{"n":12,"displayN":12,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"How much was the refundable deposit for a stall?","options":{"A":"200 dollars","B":"250 dollars","C":"450 dollars","D":"650 dollars"},"answer":"A","type":"Factual","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"a refundable deposit of 200 dollars"}],"evidenceExplanation":"a refundable deposit of 200 dollars","viExplanation":"Khoản đặt cọc có thể hoàn trả là 200 đô la, khác với giá thuê được quảng cáo là 450 đô la."},{"n":13,"displayN":13,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The word “reasonable” in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":{"A":"temporary","B":"affordable or fair","C":"legally required","D":"unexpectedly high"},"answer":"B","type":"Vocabulary","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"The amount seemed reasonable compared with the cost of a permanent shop"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The amount seemed reasonable compared with the cost of a permanent shop","viExplanation":"Reasonable ở đây mô tả mức giá hợp lý/chấp nhận được khi so với thuê một cửa hàng cố định."},{"n":14,"displayN":14,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which reaction to the rental information is NOT mentioned?","options":{"A":"Disappointment about extra cleaning costs","B":"Relief that deposits could be refunded","C":"Concern about customer numbers in a quieter location","D":"Anger that the centre required every seller to buy insurance from one company"},"answer":"D","type":"Negative Factual","evidencePhrases":[{"p":4,"text":"Some were disappointed that cleaning and electricity were not included. Others were relieved to learn that the deposit was refundable. A few worried that online adverts would not bring enough customers"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Some were disappointed that cleaning and electricity were not included. Others were relieved to learn that the deposit was refundable. A few worried that online adverts would not bring enough customers","viExplanation":"Bài nêu ba phản ứng: thất vọng, nhẹ nhõm và lo lắng. Không nhắc việc bắt buộc chọn một công ty bảo hiểm được chỉ định."},{"n":15,"displayN":15,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Why did some sellers choose the quieter corridor?","options":{"A":"They were prohibited from renting near the entrance.","B":"They believed their products could not be advertised online.","C":"They expected specialist buyers to find them despite lower foot traffic.","D":"They wanted to avoid selling to visitors at weekend events."},"answer":"C","type":"Inference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"They expected that customers looking specifically for handmade products would still find them through online adverts"}],"evidenceExplanation":"They expected that customers looking specifically for handmade products would still find them through online adverts","viExplanation":"Một số người bán tin rằng quảng cáo trực tuyến vẫn giúp khách quan tâm đến hàng thủ công tìm được gian hàng dù ở hành lang ít người qua lại."},{"n":16,"displayN":16,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which best describes Ms Le’s attitude towards the trial?","options":{"A":"Cautiously positive, while aware of financial risks","B":"Certain that every seller would earn a large profit","C":"Indifferent to applicants’ concerns about expenses","D":"Convinced the trial should be cancelled"},"answer":"A","type":"Attitude/Tone","evidencePhrases":[{"p":4,"text":"Nonetheless, the manager remained cautiously optimistic"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Nonetheless, the manager remained cautiously optimistic","viExplanation":"Cụm “cautiously optimistic” thể hiện thái độ lạc quan thận trọng, đồng thời khuyến khích người bán xem xét kỹ chi phí."},{"n":17,"displayN":17,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Where should the following sentence be inserted? “That explanation reassured applicants who had worried that the deposit was simply another rental fee.”","options":{"A":"[A]","B":"[B]","C":"[C]","D":"[D]"},"answer":"D","type":"Sentence Insertion","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"The centre explained that the deposit was held as security rather than counted as income from selling space"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The centre explained that the deposit was held as security rather than counted as income from selling space","viExplanation":"“That explanation” nhắc lại lời giải thích về mục đích của tiền đặt cọc; vì vậy câu cần chèn đứng ngay sau lời giải thích đó, tại [D]."},{"n":18,"displayN":18,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Why does the writer mention the survey about seventy percent of craft-event visitors?","options":{"A":"To prove that permanent stores are more profitable","B":"To support the idea that online information can help customers find less visible stalls","C":"To show that most visitors prefer paying in cash","D":"To criticise the shopping centre for collecting customer data"},"answer":"B","type":"Purpose","evidencePhrases":[{"p":3,"text":"approximately seventy percent of visitors who came to weekend craft events had checked stall information online before travelling"},{"p":3,"text":"to explain why location within the centre might be less important than it first appeared"}],"evidenceExplanation":"approximately seventy percent of visitors who came to weekend craft events had checked stall information online before travelling to explain why location within the centre might be less important than it first appeared","viExplanation":"Số liệu khảo sát hỗ trợ lập luận rằng nhiều khách tìm gian hàng qua mạng, nên vị trí đẹp ở trung tâm có thể không quan trọng như dự đoán."},{"n":19,"displayN":19,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The phrase “the additional costs” in paragraph 2 refers mainly to ______.","options":{"A":"the original advertised rent","B":"expected profits from weekend sales","C":"insurance, electricity and cleaning charges","D":"the price of handmade products"},"answer":"C","type":"Reference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"Insurance, electricity and a share of the weekend cleaning service were separate expenses"},{"p":1,"text":"the additional costs changed their budgets"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Insurance, electricity and a share of the weekend cleaning service were separate expenses the additional costs changed their budgets","viExplanation":"“The additional costs” quy chiếu về ba khoản phát sinh vừa được liệt kê: bảo hiểm, điện và vệ sinh cuối tuần."},{"n":20,"displayN":20,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which sentence best completes the final paragraph’s message?","options":{"A":"The cheapest advertised option is always the most profitable.","B":"Renting a shop is safer than saving money in a bank.","C":"A short contract removes all financial risks for sellers.","D":"A sound decision depends on understanding the complete financial picture."},"answer":"D","type":"Text Organization/Completion","evidencePhrases":[{"p":5,"text":"Sellers who understand what they must pay, what they might earn and which risks they can manage"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Sellers who understand what they must pay, what they might earn and which risks they can manage","viExplanation":"Đoạn kết nhấn mạnh phải xem đồng thời chi phí, thu nhập kỳ vọng và rủi ro, không quyết định chỉ dựa trên giá thuê quảng cáo."},{"n":61,"displayN":1,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"without signing a long rental contract\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"without selling anything to customers","B":"without obtaining permission from a landlord","C":"without committing to a lengthy lease","D":"without paying for electricity"},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: without committing to a lengthy lease","viExplanation":""},{"n":62,"displayN":2,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"an inexpensive-looking advert for space can hide significant expenses\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"An attractive advertised rent may conceal other substantial costs.","B":"Advertising automatically reduces the rent paid by sellers.","C":"Cheap-looking adverts are legally required to be false.","D":"Temporary retail spaces never involve extra expenses."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: An attractive advertised rent may conceal other substantial costs.","viExplanation":""},{"n":63,"displayN":3,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"The deposit would be returned after the trial if the stall was left in good condition\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The deposit would always become part of the rent.","B":"The centre would refund the security money when the stall met the return conditions.","C":"The deposit could only be used to buy products.","D":"The deposit would be refunded before the trial started."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The centre would refund the security money when the stall met the return conditions.","viExplanation":""},{"n":64,"displayN":4,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a lower headline price automatically represented better value for money\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The advertised price was the only relevant cost.","B":"Cheaper locations must generate more customers.","C":"The manager believed every expensive location was superior.","D":"A cheaper advertised figure necessarily meant a better overall deal."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A cheaper advertised figure necessarily meant a better overall deal.","viExplanation":""},{"n":65,"displayN":5,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"A quieter corridor was less expensive to operate and provided secure storage\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The less busy location reduced operating costs and offered protected storage.","B":"The corridor had the highest costs but the largest number of visitors.","C":"Storage was unavailable in the quieter location.","D":"The corridor was free because it attracted fewer shoppers."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The less busy location reduced operating costs and offered protected storage.","viExplanation":""},{"n":66,"displayN":6,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"customers looking specifically for handmade products would still find them through online adverts\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Only walk-in customers could locate handmade stalls.","B":"Advertisements had no effect on specialist buyers.","C":"Targeted shoppers could discover the stalls through online information.","D":"Handmade products could not be promoted on the internet."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Targeted shoppers could discover the stalls through online information.","viExplanation":""},{"n":67,"displayN":7,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"location within the centre might be less important than it first appeared\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"All positions in the centre had exactly the same rent.","B":"A stall's position might matter less than people originally assumed.","C":"The position of a shop never influences sales.","D":"Only the entrance location could attract online shoppers."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A stall's position might matter less than people originally assumed.","viExplanation":""},{"n":68,"displayN":8,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"compare their likely earnings with all expenses\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Estimate revenue without looking at fees.","B":"Consider only how much stock has been purchased.","C":"Ask customers to pay every business expense.","D":"Weigh expected income against the full range of costs."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Weigh expected income against the full range of costs.","viExplanation":""},{"n":69,"displayN":9,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"the manager remained cautiously optimistic\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The manager was hopeful but aware that difficulties could arise.","B":"The manager was certain every trader would make a fortune.","C":"The manager expected the trial to fail without exception.","D":"The manager refused to answer applicants' questions."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The manager was hopeful but aware that difficulties could arise.","viExplanation":""},{"n":70,"displayN":10,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a realistic budget requires more than one figure\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Only the rental fee needs to appear in a budget.","B":"Forecasting a business budget is unnecessary.","C":"A useful budget must include several kinds of financial information.","D":"A single advertised price is always a complete financial plan."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A useful budget must include several kinds of financial information.","viExplanation":""}]},{"id":3,"level":"B2","title":"Passage 3 — The Price Of Delivery Convenience","teacherTitle":"The Price Of Delivery Convenience","wordCountTarget":null,"paragraphs":["A customer ordering a new pair of shoes may see two buttons at the online checkout: standard delivery at no extra charge and express delivery for a small fee. The word “free” makes the first choice sound costless. Some customers have become so accustomed to the promise of immediate delivery that they no longer think about the trucks, warehouse staff and packaging materials behind the screen. Yet vehicles, packaging and labour are needed for both services. Someone must pay, and some costs are carried by the wider community rather than appearing on the customer's receipt.","Last year, a neighbourhood group in a large city noticed delivery vans stopping repeatedly along a narrow street. Residents complained about noise, traffic and waste from single-use packaging. Several shops replied that their customers increasingly expected delivery on demand and that competing brands offered similar services. [A] Each company was trying to keep its prices attractive, while the street as a whole was experiencing the combined effects of all those deliveries. [B]","The problem is not simply that home delivery is worse than shopping in person. A single van carrying many orders along a planned route may be more economical than twenty customers driving separately to different stores. On the other hand, repeated unsuccessful deliveries and individual express journeys can cancel that advantage. The environmental effect depends on distances, route planning, packaging and what customers would otherwise have done. [C] As a result, a cheap delivery fee is not a reliable measure of the total cost of a purchase. [D]","Retailers have begun testing alternative systems. Some offer a discount to customers who collect several purchases from a local point. Others encourage buyers to choose a slower delivery window so that more orders can travel together. These services are increasingly in demand among shoppers who want convenient delivery without unnecessary transport. Yet the benefits depend on participation: if too few people use a collection point, operating it can create additional journeys rather than reducing them.","City officials have also considered requiring large delivery firms to publish information about vehicle use and packaging waste. Critics argue that collecting these figures would be a financial burden for small businesses. Supporters respond that transparent information may reveal opportunities to save fuel and improve service. The mayor described the proposal as a first step rather than a complete solution. The policy would not ban fast delivery or impose the same route on every business.","The debate exposes a familiar difficulty in personal finance and environmental policy: the price paid by one customer does not always reflect the costs created by a system. Telling consumers to avoid all online purchases would be simplistic, just as offering every delivery for free would conceal important trade-offs. Better choices require clear information, suitable alternatives and cooperation among customers, retailers and city authorities."],"references":[{"p":3,"start":235,"end":249,"text":"These services"}],"questions":[{"n":21,"displayN":21,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What is implied by the statement that “Someone must pay” for delivery?","options":{"A":"All customers must make a separate cash payment.","B":"The actual costs may exist even when no fee appears at checkout.","C":"Only delivery workers are responsible for transport expenses.","D":"Express delivery can never be cheaper than standard delivery."},"answer":"B","type":"Restatement","evidencePhrases":[{"p":0,"text":"Yet vehicles, packaging and labour are needed for both services"},{"p":0,"text":"some costs are carried by the wider community"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Yet vehicles, packaging and labour are needed for both services some costs are carried by the wider community","viExplanation":"Dù ghi miễn phí giao hàng, chi phí vận chuyển, bao bì và lao động vẫn tồn tại; một phần chi phí có thể chuyển sang cộng đồng."},{"n":22,"displayN":22,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Why does the writer describe the neighbourhood residents’ complaints?","options":{"A":"To introduce an example of costs experienced beyond the buyer and retailer","B":"To demonstrate that online shopping has already been prohibited","C":"To argue that only small stores should provide delivery","D":"To explain why all delivery workers oppose route planning"},"answer":"A","type":"Purpose","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"Residents complained about noise, traffic and waste from single-use packaging"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Residents complained about noise, traffic and waste from single-use packaging","viExplanation":"Ví dụ về khu dân cư cho thấy các tác động tập thể của dịch vụ giao hàng, vốn không phản ánh trên hóa đơn của từng khách."},{"n":23,"displayN":23,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The phrase “in demand” in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":{"A":"temporarily prohibited","B":"no longer affordable","C":"requested or wanted by many people","D":"available only at a luxury price"},"answer":"C","type":"Vocabulary","evidencePhrases":[{"p":3,"text":"These services are increasingly in demand among shoppers"}],"evidenceExplanation":"These services are increasingly in demand among shoppers","viExplanation":"“In demand” có nghĩa là đang được nhiều người cần hoặc tìm kiếm, không phải chỉ nói về giá."},{"n":24,"displayN":24,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What is the main idea of paragraph 3?","options":{"A":"Individual shoppers always create less pollution than delivery vans.","B":"Standard delivery is environmentally harmless in every situation.","C":"Distance is the only factor that determines delivery costs.","D":"The impact of delivery depends on how the service is organised and used."},"answer":"D","type":"Main Idea","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"The environmental effect depends on distances, route planning, packaging and what customers would otherwise have done"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The environmental effect depends on distances, route planning, packaging and what customers would otherwise have done","viExplanation":"Đoạn 3 so sánh các mô hình giao hàng; tác động môi trường phụ thuộc vào cách tổ chức chứ không phải mọi hình thức giao tại nhà đều xấu."},{"n":25,"displayN":25,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The phrase “These services” in paragraph 4 refers to ______.","options":{"A":"collection-point discounts and slower combined delivery options","B":"delivery vehicles that stop on narrow streets","C":"official reports about packaging waste","D":"new regulations proposed by the mayor"},"answer":"A","type":"Reference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":3,"text":"Some offer a discount to customers who collect several purchases from a local point. Others encourage buyers to choose a slower delivery window"},{"p":3,"text":"These services are increasingly in demand"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Some offer a discount to customers who collect several purchases from a local point. Others encourage buyers to choose a slower delivery window These services are increasingly in demand","viExplanation":"“These services” chỉ hai giải pháp vừa nêu: nhận hàng tại điểm tập kết và chọn khung giao hàng chậm để ghép đơn."},{"n":26,"displayN":26,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Where should the following sentence be inserted? “A lower price on the screen, however, does not tell customers how many journeys were needed to fulfil their order.”","options":{"A":"[A]","B":"[B]","C":"[C]","D":"[D]"},"answer":"C","type":"Sentence Insertion","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"The environmental effect depends on distances, route planning, packaging and what customers would otherwise have done"},{"p":2,"text":"As a result, a cheap delivery fee is not a reliable measure of the total cost"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The environmental effect depends on distances, route planning, packaging and what customers would otherwise have done As a result, a cheap delivery fee is not a reliable measure of the total cost","viExplanation":"Câu cần chèn đề cập giá thấp trên màn hình chưa phản ánh số chuyến vận chuyển. Đặt tại [C] tạo cầu nối logic với kết luận mở đầu bằng “As a result”."},{"n":27,"displayN":27,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What is the writer’s attitude towards the proposed city reporting rule?","options":{"A":"Completely dismissive because no figures could be useful","B":"Uncritically supportive of strict bans on delivery","C":"Cautiously receptive while recognising concerns about cost","D":"Certain it would eliminate packaging waste immediately"},"answer":"C","type":"Attitude/Tone","evidencePhrases":[{"p":4,"text":"Critics argue that collecting these figures would be a financial burden for small businesses"},{"p":4,"text":"Supporters respond that transparent information may reveal opportunities to save fuel"},{"p":4,"text":"a first step rather than a complete solution"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Critics argue that collecting these figures would be a financial burden for small businesses Supporters respond that transparent information may reveal opportunities to save fuel a first step rather than a complete solution","viExplanation":"Người viết ghi nhận cả lợi ích và lo ngại, xem quy định là bước khởi đầu chứ không phải giải pháp toàn diện, nên có thái độ ủng hộ thận trọng."},{"n":28,"displayN":28,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The word “economical” in paragraph 3 most nearly means ______.","options":{"A":"highly fashionable","B":"using resources efficiently","C":"requiring luxury equipment","D":"free of any tax"},"answer":"B","type":"Vocabulary","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"A single van carrying many orders along a planned route may be more economical than twenty customers driving separately"}],"evidenceExplanation":"A single van carrying many orders along a planned route may be more economical than twenty customers driving separately","viExplanation":"Economical trong bối cảnh này là sử dụng ít nguồn lực/chi phí hơn khi gộp chuyến, thay vì chỉ nói về món hàng rẻ."},{"n":29,"displayN":29,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which tone best characterises the passage as a whole?","options":{"A":"Humorous and dismissive","B":"Angry and accusatory","C":"Celebratory and promotional","D":"Analytical and concerned with trade-offs"},"answer":"D","type":"Attitude/Tone","evidencePhrases":[{"p":5,"text":"Telling consumers to avoid all online purchases would be simplistic, just as offering every delivery for free would conceal important trade-offs"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Telling consumers to avoid all online purchases would be simplistic, just as offering every delivery for free would conceal important trade-offs","viExplanation":"Giọng văn có tính phân tích vì cân nhắc lợi ích và bất lợi của nhiều lựa chọn, không chỉ trích cực đoan hay quảng bá một giải pháp."},{"n":30,"displayN":30,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which message does the writer most strongly convey?","options":{"A":"Responsible delivery choices need transparent costs and workable alternatives.","B":"Customers should be legally required to collect every order.","C":"Shopping centres are the only source of transport pollution.","D":"Retailers can solve all delivery problems by lowering prices."},"answer":"A","type":"Main Idea","evidencePhrases":[{"p":5,"text":"Better choices require clear information, suitable alternatives and cooperation among customers, retailers and city authorities"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Better choices require clear information, suitable alternatives and cooperation among customers, retailers and city authorities","viExplanation":"Thông điệp cuối bài là muốn lựa chọn giao hàng có trách nhiệm cần minh bạch chi phí và có phương án thay thế khả thi."},{"n":71,"displayN":1,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"some costs are carried by the wider community rather than appearing on the customer's receipt\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Every delivery cost is listed on the buyer's receipt.","B":"Certain delivery costs affect society without being charged directly to the buyer.","C":"Only the retailer can experience the effects of delivery.","D":"Community members receive a discount whenever deliveries occur."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Certain delivery costs affect society without being charged directly to the buyer.","viExplanation":""},{"n":72,"displayN":2,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"delivery vans stopping repeatedly along a narrow street\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Delivery vehicles making frequent stops on a restricted road.","B":"Customers collecting parcels from a large station.","C":"Trucks moving directly to a distant warehouse without stopping.","D":"Buses transporting shoppers between two shopping centres."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Delivery vehicles making frequent stops on a restricted road.","viExplanation":""},{"n":73,"displayN":3,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"the street as a whole was experiencing the combined effects of all those deliveries\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"One household was responsible for every delivery problem.","B":"No local residents were affected by delivery traffic.","C":"Delivery firms had eliminated all traffic concerns.","D":"The neighbourhood was affected by the cumulative impact of many deliveries."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The neighbourhood was affected by the cumulative impact of many deliveries.","viExplanation":""},{"n":74,"displayN":4,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"A single van carrying many orders along a planned route may be more economical\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Every customer should drive to a separate store.","B":"Delivery routes should never be planned in advance.","C":"A well-organised van trip with multiple parcels may use resources efficiently.","D":"One van is always more costly than many separate journeys."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A well-organised van trip with multiple parcels may use resources efficiently.","viExplanation":""},{"n":75,"displayN":5,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"repeated unsuccessful deliveries and individual express journeys can cancel that advantage\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The benefits of shared delivery may disappear when trips are inefficient or repeated.","B":"Express delivery always eliminates vehicle emissions.","C":"A failed delivery never adds extra transport.","D":"Separate urgent deliveries guarantee lower costs."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The benefits of shared delivery may disappear when trips are inefficient or repeated.","viExplanation":""},{"n":76,"displayN":6,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a cheap delivery fee is not a reliable measure of the total cost of a purchase\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The listed delivery charge includes every environmental impact.","B":"Low delivery charges do not necessarily reveal the full costs involved.","C":"All online purchases have exactly the same transport cost.","D":"A low delivery fee means a product cannot be returned."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Low delivery charges do not necessarily reveal the full costs involved.","viExplanation":""},{"n":77,"displayN":7,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"more orders can travel together\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Each order must travel on a different vehicle.","B":"Customers must collect all orders within one hour.","C":"Retailers can eliminate the need for packaging.","D":"Several purchases can be transported in one shared journey."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Several purchases can be transported in one shared journey.","viExplanation":""},{"n":78,"displayN":8,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"the benefits depend on participation\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"A scheme works equally well even if nobody uses it.","B":"The scheme saves resources simply because it exists.","C":"Whether the service is useful depends partly on how many people use it.","D":"Only delivery workers determine the programme's effectiveness."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Whether the service is useful depends partly on how many people use it.","viExplanation":""},{"n":79,"displayN":9,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"The mayor described the proposal as a first step rather than a complete solution\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The mayor saw the plan as an initial measure, not a final answer.","B":"The mayor announced that delivery traffic had disappeared.","C":"The mayor rejected all future changes to delivery policy.","D":"The mayor considered the proposal sufficient to solve every problem."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The mayor saw the plan as an initial measure, not a final answer.","viExplanation":""},{"n":80,"displayN":10,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"the price paid by one customer does not always reflect the costs created by a system\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The buyer always pays every cost created by delivery.","B":"A customer's payment can fail to capture broader system-wide consequences.","C":"Retailers never bear any costs beyond the advertised price.","D":"The system has no costs unless a customer requests fast delivery."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A customer's payment can fail to capture broader system-wide consequences.","viExplanation":""}]},{"id":4,"level":"B2–B2+","title":"Passage 4 — When A Payment App Becomes A Financial Adviser","teacherTitle":"When A Payment App Becomes A Financial Adviser","wordCountTarget":null,"paragraphs":["For many young adults, a payment app is no longer simply a digital wallet. It records purchases, displays an account balance and sometimes recommends how much users should save. Developers argue that these features can make financial decisions clearer. Critics ask whether a system designed to make spending effortless is equally well equipped to encourage restraint.","A university research team recently followed 120 volunteers over six weeks. All participants could view their transaction histories, but half also received a weekly summary grouping expenses into categories such as food, travel and entertainment. The researchers did not lend anyone money or set a compulsory spending limit. At the end of the trial, the group receiving summaries was better at estimating its recent nonessential spending. Nevertheless, the researchers found no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts.","One explanation is that noticing a problem does not automatically give someone the resources to solve it. A student living on a very small budget may struggle to get by even while recording every payment. Inflation can raise the price of essentials, and a delayed wage payment can make an otherwise reasonable plan impossible to follow. Knowledge helps people understand their situation, but it cannot remove an expense that must be paid.","Technology companies are trying a different approach: giving users warnings before certain purchases. For example, a customer who sets a monthly entertainment budget may receive a message before buying another streaming subscription. These alerts can create a moment for reconsideration. However, they do not know whether the purchase has genuine personal value. A family might deliberately exceed its budget to replace an essential computer for a student's course. An automatic warning may be useful, but it should not become a moral judgment.","There is also a commercial conflict. Some apps earn a fee when users make payments or select financial products. The same company may therefore profit from more transactions while claiming to promote careful spending. Transparent information about charges can reduce this tension, but only if users can understand it. Small print stating that an offer may lead to debt is less helpful than a clear comparison of repayment costs. The absence of a warning should not be mistaken for permission to spend without thinking.","Consumer researchers have proposed several safeguards. They recommend easy-to-read fee summaries, optional reminders, the ability to review past purchases and controls that do not pressure users to accept a loan. They do not suggest banning debit cards, requiring every user to share private income details or replacing financial education with software. Technology may support decisions, but it cannot know every person's priorities.","The strongest argument for payment apps is therefore not that they make people wealthier. It is that they can provide timely information to help people exercise judgment. A useful app makes both spending and its consequences visible. Whether that improves financial wellbeing depends on what users can afford, how information is presented and whether the design respects their freedom to choose."],"references":[{"p":0,"start":200,"end":214,"text":"these features"}],"questions":[{"n":31,"displayN":31,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The phrase “these features” in paragraph 1 refers to ______.","options":{"A":"records of purchases, balance displays and savings suggestions","B":"advertisements for luxurious products","C":"government rules on repayment","D":"the volunteers in a research project"},"answer":"A","type":"Reference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":0,"text":"It records purchases, displays an account balance and sometimes recommends how much users should save"},{"p":0,"text":"these features can make financial decisions clearer"}],"evidenceExplanation":"It records purchases, displays an account balance and sometimes recommends how much users should save these features can make financial decisions clearer","viExplanation":"“These features” chỉ các chức năng vừa liệt kê: ghi nhận chi tiêu, hiển thị số dư và gợi ý tiết kiệm."},{"n":32,"displayN":32,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What did the research team find after six weeks?","options":{"A":"The summary group had twice as much savings as the other group.","B":"All participants reduced their total spending by half.","C":"The summary group estimated recent nonessential spending more accurately.","D":"The team had successfully removed the cost of essential purchases."},"answer":"C","type":"Factual","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"the group receiving summaries was better at estimating its recent nonessential spending"},{"p":1,"text":"no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts"}],"evidenceExplanation":"the group receiving summaries was better at estimating its recent nonessential spending no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts","viExplanation":"Nhóm có bảng tổng hợp ước lượng chi tiêu không thiết yếu chính xác hơn, nhưng chưa có bằng chứng họ giữ lại nhiều tiền hơn."},{"n":33,"displayN":33,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"The phrase “get by” in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":{"A":"make a fortune quickly","B":"manage with limited money","C":"purchase products on demand","D":"pay off a large loan immediately"},"answer":"B","type":"Vocabulary","evidencePhrases":[{"p":2,"text":"A student living on a very small budget may struggle to get by even while recording every payment"}],"evidenceExplanation":"A student living on a very small budget may struggle to get by even while recording every payment","viExplanation":"“Get by” nghĩa là xoay xở trang trải cuộc sống với nguồn tiền hạn chế."},{"n":34,"displayN":34,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which statement about the university study is NOT true?","options":{"A":"It lasted six weeks.","B":"It included 120 volunteers.","C":"Every participant could inspect transaction history.","D":"Researchers required a compulsory spending limit."},"answer":"D","type":"Negative Factual","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"The researchers did not lend anyone money or set a compulsory spending limit"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The researchers did not lend anyone money or set a compulsory spending limit","viExplanation":"Đề hỏi mệnh đề KHÔNG đúng. Nhóm nghiên cứu không bắt buộc người tham gia phải chịu giới hạn chi tiêu."},{"n":35,"displayN":35,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What does “The absence of a warning should not be mistaken for permission” mean?","options":{"A":"Not receiving an alert does not remove the need to judge a purchase.","B":"Apps must obtain government approval before sending alerts.","C":"A payment without an alert cannot be recorded correctly.","D":"Customers should ignore all information about fees."},"answer":"A","type":"Restatement","evidencePhrases":[{"p":4,"text":"The absence of a warning should not be mistaken for permission to spend without thinking"}],"evidenceExplanation":"The absence of a warning should not be mistaken for permission to spend without thinking","viExplanation":"Không nhận được cảnh báo từ ứng dụng không có nghĩa khoản mua sắm đã được xác nhận là hợp lý; người dùng vẫn phải tự cân nhắc."},{"n":36,"displayN":36,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which approach would the writer most likely support?","options":{"A":"Using complicated fee information that most users will ignore","B":"Encouraging people to take loans whenever an app recommends one","C":"Providing clear optional warnings while preserving user choice","D":"Replacing budgeting lessons with automatic spending restrictions"},"answer":"C","type":"Inference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":5,"text":"They recommend easy-to-read fee summaries, optional reminders"},{"p":6,"text":"whether the design respects their freedom to choose"}],"evidenceExplanation":"They recommend easy-to-read fee summaries, optional reminders whether the design respects their freedom to choose","viExplanation":"Tác giả thiên về thông tin rõ ràng và lời nhắc tùy chọn, nhưng vẫn tôn trọng quyền quyết định của người sử dụng."},{"n":37,"displayN":37,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"What can be inferred about the relationship between financial knowledge and savings?","options":{"A":"Knowing about spending guarantees a larger account balance.","B":"Information is helpful, but financial circumstances still matter.","C":"People with low incomes are less capable of understanding budgets.","D":"A payment app is more important than earnings or essential costs."},"answer":"B","type":"Inference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts"},{"p":2,"text":"Knowledge helps people understand their situation, but it cannot remove an expense that must be paid"}],"evidenceExplanation":"no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts Knowledge helps people understand their situation, but it cannot remove an expense that must be paid","viExplanation":"Biết rõ các khoản chi giúp nâng cao nhận thức nhưng hoàn cảnh thu nhập và chi phí thiết yếu vẫn ảnh hưởng đến khả năng tiết kiệm."},{"n":38,"displayN":38,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a proposed safeguard?","options":{"A":"Plain-language summaries of fees","B":"Optional spending reminders","C":"Access to past purchase records","D":"Mandatory sharing of private salary documents with retailers"},"answer":"D","type":"Negative Factual","evidencePhrases":[{"p":5,"text":"They recommend easy-to-read fee summaries, optional reminders, the ability to review past purchases"},{"p":5,"text":"They do not suggest banning debit cards, requiring every user to share private income details"}],"evidenceExplanation":"They recommend easy-to-read fee summaries, optional reminders, the ability to review past purchases They do not suggest banning debit cards, requiring every user to share private income details","viExplanation":"Ba biện pháp đầu được đề xuất rõ ràng; việc bắt buộc chia sẻ chi tiết thu nhập cá nhân lại bị bác bỏ."},{"n":39,"displayN":39,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"Which conclusion is best supported by the passage?","options":{"A":"App features may improve awareness without necessarily increasing savings.","B":"A weekly summary ensures every user avoids debt.","C":"More transactions always demonstrate stronger financial health.","D":"All digital payment providers oppose financial education."},"answer":"A","type":"Inference","evidencePhrases":[{"p":1,"text":"better at estimating its recent nonessential spending"},{"p":1,"text":"no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts"}],"evidenceExplanation":"better at estimating its recent nonessential spending no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts","viExplanation":"Thử nghiệm cho thấy chức năng ứng dụng có thể giúp nhận thức rõ chi tiêu mà chưa chắc làm số dư tiết kiệm tăng lên."},{"n":40,"displayN":40,"section":"Reading Questions","text":"How is the passage mainly organised?","options":{"A":"A history of banks followed by definitions of currencies","B":"A list of shopping advertisements followed by price comparisons","C":"A question about app benefits, evidence and limitations, then qualified recommendations","D":"A debate about taxation followed by a complete government policy"},"answer":"C","type":"Text Organization/Completion","evidencePhrases":[{"p":0,"text":"Critics ask whether a system designed to make spending effortless is equally well equipped to encourage restraint"},{"p":5,"text":"Consumer researchers have proposed several safeguards"},{"p":6,"text":"The strongest argument for payment apps is therefore not that they make people wealthier"}],"evidenceExplanation":"Critics ask whether a system designed to make spending effortless is equally well equipped to encourage restraint Consumer researchers have proposed several safeguards The strongest argument for payment apps is therefore not that they make people wealthier","viExplanation":"Văn bản mở bằng câu hỏi, phân tích nghiên cứu và hạn chế của ứng dụng, rồi đưa ra biện pháp bảo vệ và kết luận có điều kiện."},{"n":81,"displayN":1,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a payment app is no longer simply a digital wallet\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Payment apps can do more than hold and transfer digital money.","B":"Payment apps are no longer able to process transactions.","C":"Digital wallets are used only by banks.","D":"Modern apps cannot display previous transactions."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Payment apps can do more than hold and transfer digital money.","viExplanation":""},{"n":82,"displayN":2,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"a system designed to make spending effortless is equally well equipped to encourage restraint\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"An app that makes buying easy must always stop unnecessary purchases.","B":"The ability to facilitate spending may not mean an app can promote self-control equally well.","C":"All payment apps prevent users from spending their earnings.","D":"A digital wallet should never provide financial information."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The ability to facilitate spending may not mean an app can promote self-control equally well.","viExplanation":""},{"n":83,"displayN":3,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"half also received a weekly summary grouping expenses into categories\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Every volunteer received a loan each week.","B":"Half the volunteers were prevented from making purchases.","C":"Some participants received a regular breakdown of their spending by type.","D":"Volunteers could not view their own transactions."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Some participants received a regular breakdown of their spending by type.","viExplanation":""},{"n":84,"displayN":4,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"no consistent difference between the groups in how much money remained in their accounts\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The two groups had exactly identical incomes.","B":"The summary group always saved more money.","C":"No one had any money left by the end.","D":"The researchers found no reliable group-level gap in remaining balances."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The researchers found no reliable group-level gap in remaining balances.","viExplanation":""},{"n":85,"displayN":5,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"noticing a problem does not automatically give someone the resources to solve it\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Recognising a financial difficulty does not necessarily provide the means to fix it.","B":"Knowing about expenses guarantees an increase in income.","C":"Awareness removes the need to pay essential bills.","D":"People cannot understand problems unless they use apps."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Recognising a financial difficulty does not necessarily provide the means to fix it.","viExplanation":""},{"n":86,"displayN":6,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"An automatic warning may be useful, but it should not become a moral judgment\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Every spending alert should tell users that they are irresponsible.","B":"Alerts may help, but they should not condemn people's personal decisions.","C":"Apps must automatically ban all expensive purchases.","D":"Warnings should be issued only after a purchase is complete."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Alerts may help, but they should not condemn people's personal decisions.","viExplanation":""},{"n":87,"displayN":7,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"The same company may therefore profit from more transactions while claiming to promote careful spending\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"App providers always charge no fees at all.","B":"Companies cannot benefit financially when customers spend more.","C":"A provider's commercial incentives may conflict with its advice about restraint.","D":"All apps are operated by nonprofit organisations."},"answer":"C","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: A provider's commercial incentives may conflict with its advice about restraint.","viExplanation":""},{"n":88,"displayN":8,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"Transparent information about charges can reduce this tension, but only if users can understand it\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Fees must be written in complicated legal language.","B":"Customers are responsible for interpreting unreadable terms.","C":"Any disclosure, however unclear, removes conflicts of interest.","D":"Clear, understandable fee information can help address conflicting incentives."},"answer":"D","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: Clear, understandable fee information can help address conflicting incentives.","viExplanation":""},{"n":89,"displayN":9,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"They do not suggest banning debit cards\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"The researchers are not proposing a prohibition on debit cards.","B":"The researchers want to replace all debit cards with cash.","C":"The researchers believe debit cards must be banned immediately.","D":"The researchers advise deleting every transaction record."},"answer":"A","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The researchers are not proposing a prohibition on debit cards.","viExplanation":""},{"n":90,"displayN":10,"section":"B2 Paraphrase Challenge","text":"Whether that improves financial wellbeing depends on what users can afford\nWhich sentence best restates the idea above?","options":{"A":"Having an app always makes users wealthier.","B":"The benefits depend partly on users' real financial capacity.","C":"An app can remove every essential living expense.","D":"Users' income is irrelevant to financial wellbeing."},"answer":"B","type":"","evidencePhrases":[],"evidenceExplanation":"Correct paraphrase: The benefits depend partly on users' real financial capacity.","viExplanation":""}]}];
